    verification verifierProcedureIsASkillReviewGate : Test { :>> id = "9af4f03d-532d-44f8-8977-78a1f6a67bd1"; :>> title = "Sprint 664 review gate — three passes per D0172"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-11"; :>> createdBy = "claudeOpus5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Delivered: the verifier's procedure is one file that can be corrected once, the mandate is its first section, and the honesty checks a receipt owes are a table rather than a memory. The DoD's live case is this sprint's own verification: the dispatch carries the skill name and the sprint's inputs only, and the receipt it produces is what the recorder writes from. Not delivered: no harness-level control refuses a tree write from a read-only subagent - D0438's rationale names that as what would change it, and it would be a CHANGE to the Agent tool set, not a skill. The recorder's mandate (dcDelegatedCeremonyIsASkill, Low) is the other half and stays where the frontier has it."; }
